From c1ea766c5dbd9da41e2a9b96e2ac0ae5408c15d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 08:18:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: expose typed address-manager endpoint and bucket
 lifecycle

Convert all14 direct addrman legacy producers while retaining original levels,
text, locks, decisions and assertions. Existing CService/CNetAddr snapshots move
ordinary endpoint formatting to the consumer. Internal bucket/count diagnostics
remain signed; ASmap groups have no false peer-AS standards mapping. The rare
missing-collider conditional retains its existing producer string/empty branch.
One LOG_TIME producer remains explicitly deferred in the coverage inventory.

Add real AddrMan state/JSON fixture covering add,new/tried selection,promotion
and getaddr, plus a one-node RPC persistence regression. Native/runtime checks
pending a coordinated combined batch. AST16/source355/Ruff and diff checks pass.

Scripted diff (ast-grep-py0.51.0 reviewed exact mappings):
/private/tmp/lane-n4-build/logging-compose/ast-venv/bin/python contrib/logging/conversion/convert.py --rules contrib/logging/conversion/rules/address-manager-lifecycle.json --report /Users/shammah/repos/lotus-v2-repair-work/logging-cleanup/addrman-applied.json --apply
git clang-format --force --binary /opt/homebrew/bin/clang-format --style '{BasedOnStyle: InheritParentConfig, BreakStringLiterals: false}' HEAD -- src/addrman.cpp src/test/logging_event_tests.cpp

Manual native/functional tests and explicit include/registry support adjustments
reviewed separately; no production behavior outside logging changed.
